ust like  an error training graph versus narrative  radiograph with a planted clique there's  this there's this very strong conjecture  floating around that says that's  actually you know if low degree  polynomials don't solve the problem then  polynomial time algorithms don't solve  the problem  and i would love to establish some  version of this conjecture  unconditionally  when you restrict from convex from  polynomial time algorithms to some of  square's convex programs we could hope  to unconditionally rule out these  powerful algorithms under a very mild uh  criterion on uh on an underlying  hypothesis testing problem so a major  goal of mine this semester is to try to  make a little bit of progress on this  sum of squares version of the low degree  conjecture and i'm happy to talk to  people about it  um  in case there in case you don't want to  talk to me about those things you could  talk to me about discrepancy i'm super  into discrepancy recently you could talk  to me about combinatorial optimization  i've thought a little bit about  indistinguishability obfuscation and  cryptography  and i also really like to talk about and  ride bicycles so you can talk to me  about that too if all else fails  um finally a super short plug we have a  workshop on a lot of this stuff next  week uh called rigorous evidence for  information computation trade-offs  there's gonna be a lot of awesome talks  um and i promise none of the speakers  are going to invert easy and hard  problems like i did so the talks will be  super accurate  uh  great i hope to see you all there that's  all  [Applause]  thanks sam um  yeah this is a super quick question  but otherwise  people just keep that party rolling yeah

